ing\n    else:\n        # If no text found, try to find in a table structure\n        # Use get_by_role to find tables and rows with 'Pending'\n        tables = page.get_by_role(\"table\")\n        table_count = await tables.count()\n        for i in range(table_count):\n            rows = tables.nth(i).get_by_role(\"row\")\n            row_count = await rows.count()\n            for j in range(row_count):\n                row_text = await rows.nth(j).text_content()\n                if \"Pending\" in row_text:\n                    print(row_text)  # Print the row text as-is\n                    return\n        print(\"No pending reviews found\")\n</code>\n\n<exception>\n'IndentationError': unexpected indent\n</exception>\n\n---\n\n<reasoning>\nI need to find the total count of Pending reviews. Currently, I'm on the Dashboard page of Magento Admin, as shown in the accessibility tree. The tree does not contain any direct references to reviews or pending counts on this page. I must navigate to a page that contains review information. In Magento Admin, reviews are typically managed under the 'Catalog' section. The accessibility tree shows a link with role 'link' and name 'Catalog'. I should click this link to expand its menu and look for a 'Reviews' submenu item. If not found, I'll try the 'Reports' link. Once on the reviews page, I'll search for elements indicating pending reviews, such as text containing 'Pending' or table rows with status information. I must use Playwright's get_by_role and get_by_text methods, ensuring to handle any loading states. Since no knowledge base functions are provided, I'll rely on standard Playwright methods. The goal is to extract and print the pending count directly from the page content without any processing or transformation.\n</reasoning>\n\n<code>\nasync def act(page):\n    # Click on 'Catalog' link to expand its menu\n    await page.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Catalog\").click()\n    await page.wait_for_timeout(2000)  # Wait for 